{"id":"word:hebrew:H5104","type":"word","title":"נָהָר","subtitle":"H5104 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a stream (including the sea; expectation the Nile, Euphrates, etc.); figuratively, prosperity","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נָהָר (H5104) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 119 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נָהָר (nâhâr) means a stream (including the sea; expectation the Nile, Euphrates, etc.); figuratively, prosperity First listed occurrence: 1Chr 1 48."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נָהָר","transliteration":"nâhâr","pronunciation":"naw-hawr'","strong":"H5104","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5104","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["נְהַר","הַ/נָּהָ֑ר","בִּֽ/נְהַר","הַ/נָּהָר֙","הַ/נָּהָ֔ר"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmsa",32],["HNcmpa",18],["HNcmsc",17],["HNcmsa",9],["HR/Ncmsc",6],["HRd/Ncmsa",4],["HNcmpc",4],["HTd/Ncmpa",3],["HC/Ncmsa",3],["HRd/Ncmpa",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"a stream (including the sea; expectation the Nile, Euphrates, etc.); figuratively, prosperity","usage":"flood, river.","full":"H5104. nahar נָהָר noun masculine Gen 2:10 stream, river ; — absolute ׳נ 2:10 +; construct נְהַר Deut 1:7 +; plural נְהָרִים Isaiah 18:27 4 t., construct נַהֲרֵי Isa 18:1-2 t; but oftener נְהָר(וֺ)ת 19:6 23 t.; construct נַהֲרוֺת 2Kin 5:12 2 t.; suffix נַהֲרוֺהֶיךָ Ezek 32:2 , נַהֲרֹתַיִךְ Isa 44:27 , נַהֲרֹתֶיהָ Ezek 31:4 , 15 , נַהֲרֹתָם Exod 7:19 , נַהֲרוֺתָם Ezek 32:2 , 14 ; apparently dual נַהֲרַיִם Gen 24:10 2 t., נַהֲרָ֑יִם Judg 3:8 (see below) (all in נ ׳אֲרַם ); — 1 stream, river , Num 24:6 (JE), Job 14:11 ; 40:23 ; Psa 105:41 (in simile), Isa 48:18 (id.), 59:19 (id.) + often; frequently of particular rivers; r. of Eden Gen 2:10 and its branches 2:13 ; 2:14 (all J); מִצְרַיִם נְהַר 15:18 (J; i.e., si vera 1., the Nile) but read probably מ ׳נַחַל , whence נהר through influence of following נהר — compare 2Kin 24:7 — Nö ZMG xi.1886, 699 (alternative), Lag BN 140 Ball Hpt ; נָהָר of Nile Isa 19:5 ; especially of Euphrates מְּרָת נְהַר Gen 15:18 ; Deut 1:7 (both + ׳הַנּ הַגָּדוֺל ) Josh 1:4 8 t. + 2Sam 8:3 (Qr ᵐ5 and || 1Chr 18:3 ; Kt omit מְּרָת ; — compare also Gen 2:14 b above); oftener (of Euphrase) without ׃פ ׳הַנָּהָר κατ’ ἐξοχήν , 31:21 ; Exod 23:31 ; Num 22:5 ; Josh 24:2-3 , 14 , 15 (all E), possibly also Gen 36:37 (P; compare Di) = 1Chr 1:48 , + 13 t. + 2Sam 8:3 Kt (see above); and even without article (poetry) Isa 7:20 ; Jer 2:18 ; Micah 7:12 ; Zech 9:10 ; Psa 72:8 ; ׳הַנּ ׳הַגּ once of Tigris Dan 10:4 ; גוֺזָן נְהַר ( חבור ) 2Kin 17:6 ; 18:11 compare 2 Chron 5:26; plural בוּשׁ נַהֲרֵי Zeph 3:10 ; perhaps of a canal: נְהַרכְּֿבָר Ezek 1:1 , 36t. Ezekiel; אַהֲלוא הַנָּהָר Ezra 8:21 , א ׳נְהַר 8:31 ; compare בָּבֶל נַהֲרוֺת Psa 137:1 ; canals possibly also in הַנּ ׳שַׁעֲרֵי Nahum 2:7 (of Nineveh); of canals of Egypt Exod 7:19 (|| יְאֹרִים etc.), 8:1 (|| id.). 2 נְהָרוֺת ( מִבְּכִי ) Job 28:11 usually understood of (underground) streams ; Szold Comm. Job Gr Monatsschr.1887, 410 and Perles Analekten 69 proposes ׳נִבְכֵ ׳נ sources of rivers (compare 36:16 ); Wetzst Hoffm Bu ׳מַבְּכֵ ׳נ (not elsewhere) with similar meaning. 3 figurative of ׳י s favour Psa 46:5 . &#8212; On נַהֲרַיִם ending apparently dual, see אֲרַם ; Tel Amarna Na-ri-ma, Na—rima (Wkl Tel Am. 40 *), and Egyptian Nhrina (WMM As.u.Eur.249ff. ) point however to original ending יִ֯ם ; this inconsistent with view of EMey Geschichte. § 180 that יִַ֯ם here a locative ending (compare Ba § 194 c. Anm. l Buhl Ges 12 ), see also Di Gen 24:10 .","rootNote":"from 5102 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 1 48","keyReferences":["1Chr 1 48","1Chr 5 9","1Chr 5 26","1Chr 18 3","1Chr 19 16","1Kgs 5 1","1Kgs 5 4","1Kgs 5 4"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":119,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 1 48","bo